<title>GREECE: GREEK EFTE TAX WON'T BE CUT IN 1997 - GOVT SOURCE.</title>
<headline>GREEK EFTE TAX WON'T BE CUT IN 1997 - GOVT SOURCE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's 1997 draft budget will neither abolish nor reduce the banking services tax (EFTE), a government source told Reuters.</p>
<p>EFTE will be reduced gradually in the next few years starting in 1998, he said. The EFTE tax is applied to interest payments and is currently at four percent. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
